          "body": "\" 370 -// This means that the scene rect grows but doesn't shrink, which is\"  \nPersonal aversion to scroll bars. The pane stays sized to the largest diagram viewed.  \nIf working down at the bottom of a large diagram then click another packet with smaller diagram left with a blank pane until scrolling up.  \nIs there a better term than \"Refresh\" to tidy the view?  \n  \nUpdate: would a check box be better to hold scroll position and not resize?  \ne.g. The Packet Bytes `Allow hover highlighting`",
